#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/ubuntu.md:0
msgid ""
"Learn how to identify your Ubuntu version and install snap on versions or "
"flavours where it is not included by default, then test it with hello-world."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/ubuntu.md:8
msgid "Install snap on Ubuntu"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/ubuntu.md:10
msgid "Snap is pre-installed and ready to go on all recent releases of Ubuntu."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/ubuntu.md:12
msgid ""
"This means, if you're running [Ubuntu 16.04 LTS (Xenial Xerus)](https://"
"www.ubuntu.com/) or later, including [Ubuntu 22.04 LTS (Jammy Jellyfish)]"
"(https://releases.ubuntu.com/22.04/) and [Ubuntu 23.04 (Lunar Lobster)]"
"(https://old-releases.ubuntu.com/releases/lunar/), you don't need to do "
"anything."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/ubuntu.md:14
msgid ""
"If you need to know which version of Ubuntu you're running, open "
"**Settings** and select the **About** page. Alternatively, from the command "
"line, type `lsb_release -a`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/ubuntu.md:16
msgid ""
"For versions and flavours of Ubuntu that don't include *snap* by default, "
"*snap* can be installed from the Ubuntu Software Centre by searching for "
"`snapd`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/ubuntu.md:18
msgid "Alternatively, *snapd* can be installed from the command line:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/ubuntu.md:20
msgid ""
"sudo apt update\n"
"sudo apt install snapd\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/ubuntu.md:25
msgid ""
"Either log out and back in again, or restart your system, to ensure snap’s "
"paths are updated correctly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/ubuntu.md:27
msgid ""
"To test your system, install the [hello-world](https://snapcraft.io/hello-"
"world) snap and make sure it runs correctly:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/ubuntu.md:29
msgid ""
"$ sudo snap install hello-world\n"
"hello-world 6.4 from Canonical✓ installed\n"
"$ hello-world\n"
"Hello World!\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/ubuntu.md:36
msgid "Snap is now installed and ready to go."
msgstr ""
